<article class="env-lemma" id="0AZM">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AZM">Lemma <span data-tag="0AZM">43.13.1</span>.</a> Let $X$ and $Y$ be varieties. Then $X \times Y$ is a variety and $\dim (X \times Y) = \dim (X) + \dim (Y)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The scheme $X \times Y = X \times _{\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\mathbf{C})} Y$ is a variety by Varieties, Lemma <a href="/tag/05P3" data-tag="05P3">33.3.3</a>. The statement on dimension is Varieties, Lemma <a href="/tag/0B2M" data-tag="0B2M">33.20.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>